From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: h713: add the HY300 (2023 firmware) board dts

The MagCubic HY300 of issue #8: the classic HY300 case, a 720p panel at
project 0x34, the oldest ADT-3 firmware reported so far (U-Boot and ARISC
of 2023-06-25, a display.bin revision of its own) and the HY350 family's
DRAM block at 792 MHz. It gets a device tree of its own, so that the DTB a
TEST image for it boots is named after this board. Its owner cannot open
the unit; the silkscreen is unknown, and the board is named after its
firmware.

The tree is the HY300 Pro's, as the HY300 Pro's once was the HY310's: the
nearest board of the same vendor family and panel, with nothing measured
on this one. Its stock device tree (69632 bytes, a84bfbd5...) has not been
posted, so no pin of it has been compared. What the owner reports of the
case decides the one change: there is a manual focus ring and no motor, so
motor_ctr is off; with it on, the driver would home at probe and drive
PH4..PH7 into nothing. No camera, a headphone jack, one button, a remote.

Not this board's, and said so here: the display firmware's elog addresses
and the AFBD handoff words. Both belong to the display.bin revision, which
nobody has run; the tree keeps the HY300 Pro's. A wrong elog pair only
empties the elog dump. Wrong handoff words make the AFBD driver refuse
(-ENODEV) and leave the wall black after the logo, which is then the thing
to look for in the first run; the HY320 (0335) is the example of a
revision that needed its own words.

Wi-Fi is an AIC8801 (SDIO 5449:0145, read by the owner); the driver tells
the chips apart itself. Built (dtc, against the series applied to
6.18.38); not booted.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
@@ -62,6 +62,7 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-l018.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy320.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy300-t08.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy300-2023.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-h728-x96qpro+.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-t527-avaota-a1.dtb
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-2023.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-2023.dts
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy300-2023.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+/*
+ * MagCubic HY300 with the 2023-06 ADT-3 firmware (issue #8): the classic
+ * HY300 case, 1280x720 at project 0x34, DDR3 at 792 MHz (the HY350 family's
+ * block), a display.bin revision of its own. The silkscreen is unknown, the
+ * owner cannot open the unit; the board is named after its firmware.
+ *
+ * The HY300 Pro's tree, the nearest board of the same vendor family and
+ * panel, with nothing measured on this one and its stock tree not posted.
+ * One change from what the owner reports of the case: a manual focus ring
+ * and no motor, so motor_ctr is off (on, the driver would home at probe and
+ * drive PH4..PH7 into nothing). No camera; a headphone jack; one button.
+ *
+ * Not this board's: the elog addresses and the AFBD handoff words are the
+ * HY300 Pro's, because this firmware revision has never run. A wrong elog
+ * pair only empties the elog dump; wrong handoff words make the AFBD driver
+ * refuse and leave the wall black after the logo (the HY320 needed its own,
+ * 0335). That is what to look for in the first run.
+ *
+ * Wi-Fi: an AIC8801, which the driver tells apart itself. The image built
+ * from this is a TEST image for its owner.
+ */
+
+#include "sun50i-h713-hy300-pro.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "MagCubic HY300 (2023 firmware)";
+	compatible = "magcubic,hy300-2023", "allwinner,sun50i-h713";
+};
+
+/* a manual focus ring, no motor (owner, issue #8) */
+&motor_ctr {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
